module Primitives
    intent =
        "The primitives Aver has not got, declared as a contract rather than"
        "written."
        "A capability module is a contract with no body: it says what the"
        "operation means and leaves a host to supply it. Both of these are"
        "pure, which is the right shape for a hash and for a curve -- the same"
        "arguments always give the same answer, there is nothing to record and"
        "nothing to replay."
        "They are one contract rather than three because a provider binds a"
        "whole contract. One module means one contract_hash, one provider"
        "package and one line in aver.toml, and there is no case where this"
        "project would want a curve without the hashes or the other way round."
        "Bytes, because a contract may now import the standard type and cross"
        "the boundary as it -- jasisz/aver#1022 gave Bytes a compiler-owned"
        "capability ABI. It used to require every boundary type to be declared"
        "in the capability module so contract_hash could pin its layout, which"
        "meant a carrier record here and a conversion at every edge."
        "A verify case that reaches one of these operations reaches the real"
        "provider: aver builds and binds the packages named in aver.toml on"
        "its own, so every expectation here holds against libsecp256k1 and"
        "the RIPEMD-160 it ships with. Whether the provider is right is also"
        "tested in the provider's own language, against the published vectors,"
        "where the implementation actually is."
    kind = capability
    semantics = pure
    exposes [ripemd160, sha1, verifySignature, verifySchnorr, taprootTweakMatches]
    depends [Bytes]

operation ripemd160(input: Bytes) -> Bytes
    ? "The twenty-byte RIPEMD-160 digest of these bytes."
      "Bare RIPEMD-160, not OP_HASH160: the composite is Bitcoin's and is"
      "composed by the caller out of this and the SHA-256 Aver already has."

operation sha1(input: Bytes) -> Bytes
    ? "The twenty-byte SHA-1 digest of these bytes."
      "Broken as a hash and still consensus. OP_SHA1 is in the Script language"
      "and two spends on mainnet run it -- Heights 251684 and 251898 -- so an"
      "engine that cannot compute it cannot decide them. Nothing here is"
      "asking whether SHA-1 is safe; the chain settled that question by"
      "containing the opcode."

operation taprootTweakMatches(internalKey: Bytes, tweak: Bytes, outputKey: Bytes, parityOdd: Bool) -> Bool
    ? "Whether this Taproot output key is this internal key tweaked by this"
      "tweak, with this parity."
      "The one place the engine needs point arithmetic on the curve rather"
      "than signature verification. BIP341 commits to a Script tree by adding"
      "t times G to the internal key, where t is a tagged hash of the key and"
      "the Merkle root, and a script path spend proves the commitment by"
      "showing the internal key and the path rather than by signing. There is"
      "no way to check that with a verify operation, so it is its own."
      "The parity is the low bit of the control block's first byte: an x-only"
      "key does not carry the sign of its y coordinate and the spender has to"
      "supply it."
      "False means it does not match, including a tweak at or above the group"
      "order and a key that is not on the curve. Neither is a fault: a spend"
      "may contain either and the answer is the same."

operation verifySchnorr(publicKey: Bytes, signature: Bytes, message: Bytes) -> Bool
    ? "Whether this is a valid BIP340 Schnorr signature by this public key"
      "over this thirty-two byte message."
      "A different scheme from ECDSA and not a variant of it. The public key"
      "is thirty-two bytes, x-only: the y coordinate is not carried and is"
      "taken to be even, which is what makes a Taproot output key the same"
      "width as the hash it replaced. The signature is exactly sixty-four"
      "bytes with no DER framing and no trailing hash type -- a Taproot"
      "signature may carry a hash type as a sixty-fifth byte and the caller"
      "strips it before it gets here."
      "False means it does not verify. A key that is not on the curve and a"
      "signature of the wrong length are both false rather than a fault,"
      "because a spend may legitimately contain either and the answer is"
      "still that it does not verify."

operation verifySignature(publicKey: Bytes, signature: Bytes, message: Bytes) -> Bool
    ? "Whether this is a valid secp256k1 ECDSA signature by this public key"
      "over this thirty-two byte message."
      "The signature is DER without the trailing hash type byte, and the"
      "message is the signature hash, already computed. False means the"
      "signature does not verify; it does not mean the inputs were malformed,"
      "which the caller refuses before it gets here."
